  "tolerancePolicy": "Recalibrated 2026-08-10 after the reviewed Platinum raster core replaced the legacy SVG painter. Each icon uses its dedicated 32 px or 16 px Theme Lab specimen; geometry stays at 0.02 except the irregular Trash crop (0.05), edge limits are 0.5–2.4 px, and material limits are object-specific (5–120) from the pinned historical crops. These are regression ceilings, not claims of pixel identity; the fixed reference/current/overlay/difference boards remain part of visual acceptance. Two tiers, never merged: `tolerances` is the regression tier (seeded from the recorded run with a margin, so it detects drift from that run — not distance from the historical target). `floor` is the absolute tier from FIDELITY_FLOOR in tooling/theme-lab-fidelity-contract.mjs (geometry 0.05, edge 1.5px at 1x scaled by deviceScaleFactor, material 12); it is identical for every era and never derived from our own output. Every specimen must meet the floor unless its ledger names the metric under `failing` (a real gap, with its historical reason) or `exempt` (the pinned crop cannot support that metric). A `failing` metric that starts to meet the floor fails the gate until the ledger is corrected, so an improvement cannot hide behind a stale entry."
}
